\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301634} {:answer/id #uuid "103cea83-0ac6-55b7-b74f-520018d9d638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{4},\\,y\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301635} {:answer/id #uuid "1649eb62-993a-53d9-ac21-15fd06db9865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -4,\\,y\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301636} {:answer/id #uuid "13f76c90-a2ef-532c-8e65-bbfbc0885fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,y\\le -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301637} {:answer/id #uuid "9399c3c9-512a-55ec-92a6-5e8ec8edcec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -\\frac{1}{2},\\,y\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbaaf15d-e5ff-5aae-bc3e-90cdd6fa52fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -\\frac{1}{4},\\,y\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301634} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed028a5e-72fe-5f10-9681-03697bea8ccf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4387361-c86a-55f1-abee-652931e3d6d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-16149" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}+t,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-2,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2}+t \\\\  & ={(t+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & ={(t+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${(t+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\ge 0,$ we can conclude that $x\\ge -\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that ${t}^{2}\\ge 0.$ Therefore, we can conclude that $y\\ge -2.$\n\nSo, the ranges are $x\\ge -\\frac{1}{4}$ and $y\\ge -2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0dc11d5-8eda-52b1-b7b1-42b481813ff4" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Curve Defined Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f29a511c-7868-5cb1-81f4-9d3980ad8f1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/q-16190-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084820} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b68a80-cbc5-5be5-96a2-36e49ca90c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/q-16190-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084821} {:answer/id #uuid "2379493d-13ba-52ba-ad91-b4225afbf29b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/q-16190-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084822} {:answer/id #uuid "3a30a836-7cc2-59a5-864a-eadb28c0be44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/q-16190-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084823} {:answer/id #uuid "58d40a67-a2b3-5515-bb12-bf78f2155c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/q-16190-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d40a67-a2b3-5515-bb12-bf78f2155c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/803/Source/Images/q-16190-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084824} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4d696ef-f936-5306-b905-c40612d8ca41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97c9ad2f-34fd-5e92-ba59-191660c3f61f" :question/math-academy-id "q-16190" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}-2,\\,\\,\\,y=3-t,\\,-3\\le t\\le 3\n$$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x={t}^{2}-2.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=3-t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $6$ | $5$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/6a66ca74691344866c4f754edf36acc2f5301a0eeecee6340a0a701ad99f5fd6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0dc11d5-8eda-52b1-b7b1-42b481813ff4" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Curve Defined Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6745ee5c-eb7b-5dfd-b812-0c456adad682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/assets/37e263a01854edeee87bf999b493d7bf02bef33b60dee5af6740c6b9384bfd77.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262745} {:answer/id #uuid "b7693a0d-326a-53b0-a154-5c15f3815a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949104/assets/64ac74a9f74475ad5ee699293d789221776f6764e525d1e057cfbaacdbb731b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262746} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2ac2a1-d2ac-5