$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ | $25$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t(5-t).$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ | $25$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $4$ | $6$ | $6$ | $4$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/1aa848f287660c0858d5d6478da71c5baab9252c13f0a2d4a48c38d61f6bce51.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0dc11d5-8eda-52b1-b7b1-42b481813ff4" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Curve Defined Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b856d6cb-8174-5aa9-a3f8-f8dad2890a2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/ecf914db233f7b1775f49b060470af6a244f8ea8d101fdcced746144b0284552.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301641} {:answer/id #uuid "28598f38-b560-5ca5-b3e4-ce69e9681e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/f3cd046f58b44ee916b85df91382a16360895b12c8d47a4a25deffe09f7d7c05.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301642} {:answer/id #uuid "87a98be6-40dc-5031-9ee6-95c18bd52820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/9e5fb2564eb1f5adb380d70e1a86925fa377f10cc653d98d73ba64bfb03de197.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301643} {:answer/id #uuid "dcac7630-1451-5a75-957f-4817e5cdc8f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-c