.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have \n$-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 3 & \\text{ }\\ge -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -3 \\\\ -3 & \\le -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 3 \\\\ -3 & \\le y\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-3\\le y\\le 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301674 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cddc940d-2185-569c-a62b-b507e95d3c35" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation Defined in Terms of Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63407675-1f24-50c1-a1c7-8c7cbd478b82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301676} {:answer/id #uuid "af83519a-06e9-51e2-a019-5ced0a3cefa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63407675-1f24-50c1-a1c7-8c7cbd478b82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301676} :answer-field/id #uuid "539b4597-045b-5896-a9dc-35394073b8b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adedcb41-740f-5a61-93a3-2c37de01f43d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adedcb41-740f-5a61-93a3-2c37de01f43d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301679} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dabe942-2d3d-5e34-8dc8-77908fcdb115" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301678} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de89c9ed-e715-536d-89d9-6184a0