e \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -4 & \\le 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 4 \\\\ -4+1 & \\le 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1\\le 4+1 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-3\\le x\\le 5.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} & \\le -\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} & \\le y\\le \\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{7}{2}\\le y\\le \\frac{7}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cddc940d-2185-569c-a62b-b507e95d3c35" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation Defined in Terms of Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1b216b6-7d7c-5c00-9828-c9adea0fafe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1b216b6-7d7c-5c00-9828-c9adea0fafe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301691} :answer-field/id #uuid "87de71d9-a4fc-54c7-b370-ab4daf804b85" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86860cc1-47e0-5045-bef7-de6b4bbc2305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86860cc1-47e0-5045-bef7-de6b4bbc2305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301693} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c18d292-0c20-547f-8031-81a597f05eca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a93c4b4e-1d65-5dde-9ddd-cf245e61c9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a93c4b4e-1d65-5dde-9ddd-cf245e61c9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301695} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d992412-53fd-5d84-a604-82a52db10c35" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbe81d19-2720-59fd-9eef-48259811c6ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{29}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbe81d19-2720-59fd-9eef-48259811c6ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{29}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301697} :answer-field/id #uuid "966042dc-0aa8-5620-a9f5-e3f0f01a077b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301696} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5978e7f-be03-5f3a-b7b4-48156f939847" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5978e7f-be03-5f3a-b7b4-48156f939847" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301699} :answer-field/id #uuid "145c4da9-7a11-5237-a0c8-26175f599623" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce9110a0-e81d-5d92-9def-d0ddd4285922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce9110a0-e81d-5d92-9def-d0ddd4285922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301701} :answer-field/id #uuid "429a3c3d-7ef6-563f-9941-f8404ee219b6" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "228348c4-417c-5317-8a06-708e7bb1dc72" :question/math-academy-id "q-327884" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{7}{3},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is \n{{field-1}}\n$\\le x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is \n{{field-4}}\n$\\le y$\n{{field-5}}{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & \\le -\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{4}{3} & \\le \\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le \\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-1\\le x\\le \\frac{5}{3}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & \\le \\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{7}{3} & \\le \\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{7}{3}\\le \\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{29}{6} & \\le y\\le \\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{29}{6}\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261094 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512" :knowledge-point/title "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "742d4a04-2d6a-5a66-8921-e514c7ef5953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301703} {:answer/id #uuid "75c7665a-9a0f-59ce-86ed-ab1d352efacb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301704} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c98dd4-620a-5da3-9782-0b10fe6807ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301705} {:answer/id #uuid "941442e4-f07d-5399-b298-6c9b03cbbe1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301706} {:answer/id #uuid "0a827f7a-48e6-555a-b425-1ea360d661db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "941442e4-f07d-5399-b298-6c9b03cbbe1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301706} :answer-field/id #uuid "33292b44-3afa-5a9e-ad2e-3c85425208bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb6b00ad-d0da-51b8-947a-ae3a849534d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-6832" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}),\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}),\\,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0$ | $b$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $-a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\na=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (-3)}{3})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (-1)}{2})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (3)}{2})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n-a+b+c=-(-1)+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cddc940d-2185-569c-a62b-b507e95d3c35" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation Defined in Terms of Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ef42b53-c947-565c-92f4-0805416a3f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\le x\\le 5,\\,-9\\le y\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301710} {:answer/id #uuid "d29e53c2-1b0f-5cc4-97e9-ccec68455ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\le x\\le 0,\\,1\\le y\\le 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301711} {:answer/id #uuid "72f9f89e-712b-5ab7-a5c4-cc178ff9b7af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 13,\\,3\\le y\\le 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301712} {:answer/id #uuid "31684924-c9a6-510c-9776-e96f4ceef062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 5,\\,-7\\le y\\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301713} {:answer/id #uuid "969c2915-2689-5624-bfb9-1ac9afca9aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\le x\\le 6,\\,-13\\le y\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "969c2915-2689-5624-bfb9-1ac9afca9aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\le x\\le 6,\\,-13\\le y\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301714} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea0f38ba-c575-54aa-a792-f2d49224cee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2602fecb-27f9-522e-9ca3-fc225206d948" :question/math-academy-id "q-70523" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5,\\,\\,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -7,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+5 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5\\le 1+5 \\\\ 4 & \\le x\\le 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $4\\le x\\le 6.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -6 & \\le 6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 6 \\\\ -6-7 & \\le 6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -7\\le 6-7 \\\\ -13 & \\le y\\le -1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-13\\le y\\le -1.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $4\\le x\\le 6$ and $-13\\le y\\le -1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbf0ad0-a7c5-5c0f-a06c-9210fdc244ef" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2569c24-8471-5841-ae05-a7cff0f337de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -1,\\,y\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301717} {:answer/id #uuid "9de1f544-3897-5434-80f3-72b1809fd2c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 0,\\,y\\le -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301718} {:answer/id #uuid "7f55fdbf-0998-5ffc-84b0-4740eaecd447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 1,\\,y\\le -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301719} {:answer/id #uuid "cf9b6908-99a6-5fa6-9366-49caeba2a218" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 4,\\,y\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301720} {:answer/id #uuid "471a0a49-3571-53f7-bccf-3554a722e760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 2,\\,y\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "471a0a49-3571-53f7-bccf-3554a722e760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 2,\\,y\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301721} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f44bdc1-b8f6-5835-927f-3bb94ba97d65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fc2dccb-24dd-5003-b2b4-73d21d258e08" :question/math-academy-id "q-73617" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-t,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-4,\\,t\\ge -1,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $1-t\\le 2$ for all $t\\ge -1.$ Consequently, $x=1-t\\le 2.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that ${t}^{2}\\ge 0$ for all $t.$ Consequently, $y={t}^{2}-4\\ge -4.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $x\\le 2$ and $y\\ge -4.$"}]}
